  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q26-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "26",
    "prompt": "If a cyclist had travelled 5 km/h faster, she would have needed 1.5 hr less time to travel 150 km. Find the speed of the cyclist.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$20\\text{ km/h}$. Using $150=st$ and $150=(s+5)(t-1.5)$ gives $(s+25)(s-20)=0$; take the positive speed.",
      "worked": "Let $s$ be the cyclist's speed in km/h and $t$ her travel time in hours.\n$$\\begin{align*}150&=st\\\\150&=(s+5)(t-1.5)\\\\t&=\\frac{150}{s}\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute for $t$ in the second equation:\n$$\\begin{align*}150&=(s+5)\\left(\\frac{150}{s}-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\\\150s&=(s+5)\\left(150-\\frac{3}{2}s\\right)\\\\150s&=\\frac{285}{2}s+750-\\frac{3}{2}s^2\\\\s^2+5s-500&=0\\\\(s+25)(s-20)&=0\\\\s&=-25\\text{ or }20\\end{align*}$$\nSince $s>0$, the cyclist's speed is $20\\text{ km/h}$.\nCheck: $150\\div20=7.5$ h and $150\\div25=6$ h, a decrease of $1.5$ h.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 100
  },
